#. type: 標題
#: README.md:22
msgid "## Contribution Guidelines (Provisional)"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: README.md:23
msgid "These will be updated as we go, but for the time being please use the following as a guide."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: README.md:24
msgid ""
"- For large structural or policy changes, please start a discussion in Issues first.\n"
"  - Examples: changes to the directory layout, substantial rewrites of a template, changes to operational rules, and so on.\n"
"  - When proposing an improvement, state the background and the effect you expect.\n"
"- Small fixes (typos, minor wording adjustments) can be sent straight as a Pull Request (hereafter \"PR\").\n"
"- In the title and description of a PR, please state as concisely as possible *why* the change is being made.\n"
"  - Prefixing commit titles with tags such as [add], [fix], or [update] is recommended.\n"
"- Handling PRs\n"
"  - A PR is merged after review by at least one person.\n"
"  - Automated reviews such as tests and linters must be passing."
msgstr ""

#. type: 標題
#: README.md:25
msgid "## Response Targets (SLA: Service Level Agreement)"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: README.md:26
msgid "The maintainers handle Issues and Pull Requests using the following as a guide."
msgstr ""

#. type: 標題
#: README.md:27
msgid "### Response Time Targets"
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: README.md:28
msgid ""
"- First response to an Issue\n"
"  - As a rule, a comment or a label **within one to two weeks**.\n"
"- Review of a Pull Request\n"
"  - As a rule, a review or a progress comment **within two weeks**."
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: README.md:29
msgid "The above are targets only and may slip depending on the season and circumstances."
msgstr ""

#. type: 標題
#: README.md:30
msgid "### Scope of Response"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: README.md:31
msgid "The maintainers primarily handle items such as the following."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: README.md:32
msgid ""
"- Changes and improvements to the content or structure of the templates\n"
"- Unifying terminology and tidying up wording\n"
"- Adjustments to the overall direction and positioning of the OSPO Starter Kit"
msgstr ""

#. type: 段落
#: README.md:33
msgid "Conversely, the following are, as a rule, **outside the maintainers' SLA**."
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: README.md:34
msgid ""
"- Individual consulting that goes into circumstances specific to a single organization\n"
"- Troubleshooting of system settings, networks, or authentication outside this repository\n"
"- Approval or authorization of company-wide systems and governance design other than the OSPO itself\n"
"- Anything else unrelated to the content of the templates"
msgstr ""

#. type: 標題
#: README.md:35
msgid "### Assumptions About Business Days and Hours"
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: README.md:36
msgid ""
"- Business days are assumed to be **weekdays (Japan time)**.\n"
"- During busy periods or while running events, responses may take longer than the targets above."
msgstr ""

#. type: 標題
#: README.md:37
msgid "### Status of This SLA"
msgstr ""

#. type: 清單
#: README.md:38
msgid ""
"- What is described here is only \"the response the maintainers aim for\"; it is not necessarily a legally binding service guarantee.\n"
"- The content of the SLA may be reviewed and updated according to actual operations and available resources."
msgstr ""

